**Definition 3.3 (completed inputs and replay sites).** A completed source
item of $M$ is ARC Definition 5.4's unchanged choice01, actual three-block
CAP input frame, SEG-U1 occurrence/origin and all acquired dependencies.
A completed history item additionally records its imported one-bit mode
before its entire actual frame, typed outcome and received-reference
bindings. Its fixed tuple schema uses exactly these five fields: choice,
mode, frame, outcome, received bindings. A source item's type and codec
stay ARC's. Its actual choice01 and the history item's actual choice1
are the two literal type cases; any other completed-item tag is rejected.

Append a history item only after final check/ACK. Completed-cycle count
is updated at the actual outer Ready after M append and token return,
not at an earlier list-write or callback. Initial acquisition has its
separate original annotation. Current mode/frame and gate remain retained
on70 but outside the frozen predecessor M. This is no acquisition of
current request data by that earlier cover.

Add HistoryMode as one disjoint kind to ARC Definition 6.1's reservoir.
Its predicate is the represented actual version, physical PC and inlined
call site of Definition 3.1. All other kinds remain original public boot,
original private preparation, the two bootstraps, capture ingress, outer
gate, auxiliary CAP and history frame. Bootstrap/capture reservoirs use
the actual $E(L),\Delta(G_{\rm sel}),E(G_{\rm sel})$. Each earlier history
item provides exactly its mode at that site, then its frame at its frame
sites. Callback and computed command bytes are produced by literal RD/WR
work, with no external IN. The physical raw-prefix model separately retains
actually consumed current bits and an occupied IN-to-WR latch.

